Patch 3005: cellAudio tick-locked mode for rollback matches.

Symptom (two-copy rollback tests): the match desynced 30-35 s into every fight. The game's sound library advances on the audio
device clock (one block of 256 samples per notify event, paced by WASAPI or the performance counter), and the game acts on it:
a voice line that ends starts the next sound, and the pre-fight intro camera waits for one. Two PCs reached those points on ticks
1-4 apart, so the per-tick checksums differed although every input was the same.

Now: g_ps3_audio_lock_target (-1 = off, the default: paced as before) is the total number of blocks the mix thread may have mixed.
The port's rollback layer sets it to 6.25 blocks per game tick (48000 / 256 / 30) and waits for ps3_audio_lock_idle (every block
mixed, every notify queue drained and its receiver back in the receive) before the next tick runs, so the guest's audio progress is
a function of the tick on every PC. Blocks mixed for rollback re-runs are not sent to the device (g_ps3_audio_lock_mute), and
ps3_audio_lock_rewind moves every running port's read index back with a rollback (the guest memory itself is restored by the
snapshot). When the lock ends the mix thread re-bases its clock and paces on the device again. While it has
mixed every block it may, the mix thread waits on an event (ps3_audio_lock_set_target wakes it): it runs at TIME_CRITICAL, and a
Sleep(0) spin there starved a new pool thread past the snapshot thread audit (THREAD-NOT-REGISTERED, two-copy test).

Revision 2 (review of the rollback PR): the mix thread counts a block in g_ps3_audio_lock_done (release) only after audio_notify_event_queues()
returned, and ps3_audio_lock_idle reads it with acquire and reads each notify queue's active / count / waiters under the queue's own lock (the one
sys_event_queue_receive holds while it takes the event and leaves). Before, the game thread could see done == target while the last event was not
yet pushed, or a receive that had taken its event (count--) but not yet left (waiters--), and run the next tick before the guest took the block. The
step (mix, output, notify, publish) runs under a lock that ps3_audio_lock_rewind also takes, so a rewind never lands inside a block, even after the
game's 250 ms wait gave up. Test: libs/audio/tests/test_audio_lock_race.c (patch 3007).

